        "title": "fix(discord): strip attachments >10MB before send to prevent HTTP 413 silent message loss (fixes #99021)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #99021.\n\n## Changes Made\n\n1. send.shared.ts: Pre-flight size check strips attachments > 10 MB. Uses configured mediaMaxMb capped at Discord API limit.\n2. send.outbound.ts: receipt kind reflects mediaStripped flag. DEFAULT unchanged at 100.\n3. send.receipt.ts: Added mediaStripped field.\n4. 3 regression tests.\n\n## Evidence (2026-07-02T12:32:49Z, commit: 57c266490e)\n\n### Real Discord API proof (live bot)\nBEFORE: 11MB file -> HTTP 413 -> message lost\nAFTER:  Size check -> text delivered, no attachment\n  HTTP 201, Message ID: 1522195816796782666\n  Receipt kind: text (not media)\n\n### Unit tests (47/47 passed)\n- strips oversized media >10MB and sends text-only fallback\n- respects configured mediaMaxMb above Discord limit\n- sends text-only fallback with long reply text\n\n## AI Assistance\n\n- AI-assisted: Yes\n- Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
